s for it, the executor goroutine is the implementation's own loop started directly instead of by New(), and the harness reads instancesToRecover rather than letting the run loop consume it; the prerequisite prints the record's status, command presence, crtInstance and ExecedUpTo, so an unreached premise would be visible. Oracle and identity: the comparison is against whether the channel received the instance, and the identity is shared with the prerequisite. Observation path and completion: the select has a bounded alternative that prints enqueued false, so a non-observation is recorded rather than hidden, and the goroutine is stopped by the harness's deferred Shutdown flag. Contrary evidence and limits: the wall-clock grace period follows the loop's per-iteration counter rather than a clock, so the measured wait is a diagnostic; only the enqueue is observed, not the recovery it triggers; and one blocked row is exercised. No counterevidence was found that the duty fails in this scope.\\\",\n  \\\"limitations\\\":[\\\"the measured wait (~12.6s) follows the loop's one-millisecond-per-iteration counter, so it is a diagnostic rather than a specified deadline\\\",\n   \\\"the check observes the enqueue, not the recovery that consumes it, and only one blocked row is exercised\\\",\n   \\\"the executor goroutine is started by the harness rather than by epaxos.New, so the run loop's role is outside the check\\\"]}]}\njson.dump(sub,open('submission-review-c8.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nprint(sub['artifact_id'])\nPY\ncd .. && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run --submission submission-review-c8.json 2>&1 | head -8\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress