{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\": \"submission-review-c8.json\", \"summary\": \"Turn 50 reviewed the executor-timeout check, whose outcome is holds, closing the liveness question.\\n\\nState on entry. Claim C8-timeout-enqueues-blocked-instance has one artifact, 037aa44cdea4453abcd4f9d4439d1dee (executed as f01d61d7…), whose monitor outcome is holds with the oracle correspondence unreviewed. The trusted runner reproduced the observation: the prerequisite (status 0, no commands, crtInstance 0, ExecedUpTo -1) and then recovery_enqueued with enqueued true, enqueued_replica 1, enqueued_instance 0 after about 12.6 seconds. Claim C7 was confirmed this cycle as well, so the dead accept-rejection path is settled.\\n\\nReview judgement (checker_correspondence, no_issue_found). Requirement versus predicate: the claim is that a blocked instance must be enqueued for recovery once the executor's grace period elapses, and the predicate asserts enqueued == true, with the enqueued replica and instance fields independently corroborating which operation was admitted. Entry and schedule: the blocked record is built with the package's own constructor in the state a replica reaches when it has an instance number but no committed commands, the executor goroutine is the implementation's own loop started directly instead of by New(), and the harness reads instancesToRecover rather than letting the run loop consume it; the prerequisite prints the fields that would reveal an unreached premise. Oracle and identity: the comparison is against whether the channel received the instance, sharing identity with the prerequisite. Observation path and completion: the select has a bounded alternative that prints enqueued false, so a non-observation would be recorded rather than hidden, and the goroutine ends through the harness's deferred Shutdown flag. Limits are explicit: the measured wait follows the loop's per-iteration counter rather than